Z||000003||fierospeeder||12-25-2001||02:29 AM||||i wouldn't breath the air for a while.<P><BR>Yesterday, (sun) a home got burned down in illinois.  700,000 dollar house.  The son saw the xmas tree on fire, and told his parents.  When he got his parents, the tree was in much worse condition.  <BR>Once the fire dept. arrives, the house is pretty much ruined.<P>the fireman(chief), said how the young boy is a hero, because he told his parents.<P>What im thinking.  Exactly like the simpsons.  The boy accidently started the fire.  The simpson epis. is bart playing with a remote control fire truck, and it sparks a fire.  I think he hit the xmas lights or hit the outlet.  And xmas was ruined because they were robbed.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indy-2M4||12-25-2001||06:27 AM||||OMG, Aus! I hope it gets under control soon. Hope you guys are gonna be ok. I'd get that Fiero in the Garage. Have you had any hot debris land on it yet?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Kathy<BR>http:\\sofa.iwarp.com<BR>    <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IndyCrueSig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||12-25-2001||06:38 AM||||Well it is night time now and things have worsened. Our house isn't and won't be under threat (bar fallout) but the fire situation is serious.  I can see fire burning along and over the mountains about 2 miles away  70 fires are burning throughout the state. Fire fighters have been bought in from out of state and about 70 homes burnt on Christmas day (poor bastards). All roads between here and Sydney are blocked from fires, which is significant as Sydney is the largest city in the country and Wollonong is the 6th largest.<BR>Things are not looking real good.||||reg||1
